      <memberdef kind="define" id="group__dxl2__config_1ga668d14fe97878bd22dccbd6508ed916b" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>DXL2_MAX_PACKET_SIZE</name>
        <initializer>256U</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Maximum complete wire-packet size, including header and CRC, in bytes. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Sizes the parser buffer, the decoded packet and the link transmit buffer, so it directly drives the RAM footprint of one link. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/dxl2_config.h" line="63" column="9" bodyfile="inc/dxl2_config.h" bodystart="63" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Build-time configuration for DXL2. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Every parameter can be overridden by the integrator with a compiler definition (for example <computeroutput>-DDXL2_MAX_PACKET_SIZE=1024U</computeroutput>) without editing this file.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Configuration elements in this group:</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__dxl2__config_1ga668d14fe97878bd22dccbd6508ed916b" kindref="member">DXL2_MAX_PACKET_SIZE</ref> : largest wire packet the parser and encoder accept. </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
